# RX-02 Go/Rust foreign boundary result
PR: https://github.com/applicate2628/mcp-local-hub/pull/631
Head:
e0a05e3a6ec3b5ff14f3d70e935eabfda44ba445
Dependent base: #625
7ce04f7ef2f96680ed94db1edaf77cf0358421c4
Branch: spike/rx02-go-rust-boundary-20261113

Scope:10 new files only in experiments/rust-process-owner/ffi. Core/API/parent manifests/lock unchanged. Real Go/cgo/C-shim/MSVC-Rust-DLL calls into existing NativeOwner, not another process engine.
Scenario: suspended create with absolute image/cwd, EMPTY environment, no redirected stdio; one-shot allow/deny, pending/terminal finish, Job stop, terminal release. The bool decision does not implement full original-process admission evidence.

Fresh verification:8 normal Go functions zero skips; debug DLL race x3, release DLL race x3, cgocheck2, vet. Rust ABI7 unit tests debug/release, Clippy/fmt. Two explicitly tagged malformed-response checks with separate owned mutated DLLs passed; original source restored and normal DLLs rebuilt. All53 unchanged parent checks rerun debug/release plus Clippy/fmt.
TDD: no-create compiled stub failed real Go callers. New owner-transfer and release-bookkeeping defects RED/GREEN; local/native error classification RED/GREEN. Early-release and native-code-loss negative mutations detected.
General-case fixes: nonnull pointer transfer is not erased by validation error; cleared slot counts deallocation even if response metadata fails; native error code outranks broad io category; initialize output before references. No retained Go pointers/callbacks, no implicit GC cleanup/replay.

Limits: real foreign native-cleanup kernel failure not induced; mapping only ABI unit coverage plus separate parent kernel tests. No panic/allocator/loader fault isolation proof, arbitrary foreign-pointer safety or Rust/C race proof. No Unix runtime/cross-build, complete Go launch-policy parity, performance claim or product integration.
Remaining: original-process observation policy, custom env/stdio/noninheritable marshalling, cancellable blocking I/O, Unix, comparison and independent review/installation gates.
No new dependencies downloaded/installed, models/vendors/GUI invoked, merges/releases or explicit CI/bot dispatch. All new source/cache/temp/evidence D:\dev\ChatGPT.
Remote/readback and10 tested source hashes matched; own clone clean, currently on FFI branch not625. Parent commit remains unchanged.
First final core-comparison command used a malformed PowerShell range argument and printed git usage; repeated with explicit base/head arguments succeeded. This was a command error, not a source delta.
Evidence and active source retained outside trash. No confirmed unused redundant files requiring removal this increment; keep caches/targets required for continued tests.
